    7 => [
        [
            'title' => 'Verification in Remote and Hostile Areas',
            'summary' => 'Do the work where it is hardest.',
            'duration' => 60,
            'content' => "Some of the program's farms are far from the roads and the signal, and verification in remote and hostile areas is the discipline of doing the work where it is hardest.\n\nStart with the plan. The route, the fuel, the water, the charged device, and the backup power, prepared before the trip. The agent who prepares for the distance, and the day's return, is the agent who completes the visit, and the completed visit is the verification the program needs.\n\nManage the risk. Remote work carries its own hazards: the road, the weather, the terrain, and the isolation. The agent who tells someone the route and the return, and who turns back when the conditions turn, is the agent who survives the day, and the surviving agent is the one who verifies another day.\n\nAdapt the evidence. A weak signal and a slow fix need patience, and a canopy-heavy farm needs an open clearing for the GPS. The agent who adapts the capture to the conditions, and notes the limitation honestly, is the agent whose evidence survives review, and honest limits are better than fabricated precision.\n\nFinally, complete the record the same day. Remote visits are the ones most likely to be reconstructed from memory, and memory is the weakest evidence. The agent who files the record on the day, however late the night, keeps the verification true, and true verification is the agent's whole product.",
