    8 => [
        [
            'title' => 'Advisory Ethics and Boundaries',
            'summary' => 'Advise within your competence.',
            'duration' => 60,
            'content' => "The advisor's credibility rests on ethics and clear boundaries, and advisory ethics and boundaries is the discipline of advising within your competence.\n\nStart with the limits of your knowledge. The advisor who knows what they know, and what they do not, advises within their competence, and refers the rest to the specialist. The advisor who admits the limit earns the farmer's trust, and trust is the advisor's only real credential.\n\nAvoid the conflicts. The advisor who sells no product, and takes no incentive to recommend one, recommends for the farm alone. The advisor who is seen to be independent is the advisor whose advice is believed, and the believed advice is the advice that is adopted.\n\nRespect the farmer's decision. The advisor recommends; the farmer decides. The advisor who presents the options, the evidence, and the risks, and then honours the farmer's choice, keeps the relationship professional, and the professional relationship is the one that lasts.\n\nFinally, record the advice. What was recommended, on what evidence, and what was referred, written down. The advisor who records the advice protects the farmer, the advisor, and the program, and the record is the boundary that keeps the advice honest.",
