            'title' => 'Pest Management Economics',
            'summary' => 'Spend the control money wisely.',
            'duration' => 60,
            "content" => "Pest management is an investment, and pest management economics is the discipline of spending the control money wisely.\n\nStart with the cost of doing nothing. The yield lost to the pest, and the price lost to the damage, in currency. The farmer who knows the cost of doing nothing knows what the control is worth, and the control worth its cost is the control worth buying.\n\nCompare the controls. The cost, the effectiveness, and the residue, of each option. The farmer who compares the controls, and chooses the one that returns more than it costs, spends wisely, and the wise spend is the profitable control.\n\nAvoid the over-spend. The calendar spray, the double dose, and the premium product for a minor pest, all waste money. The farmer who spends only on the pest that crosses the threshold is the farmer who keeps the margin, and the kept margin is the farm's profit.\n\nFinally, measure the return. The damage before and after, and the cost of the control, recorded. The farmer who measures the return on the control knows what worked, and the known return is the farm's guide to the next season's pest management budget.",
